==Enemy==
Relic Doge is a medium-fast moving enemy with remarkably high health and attack power for a peon, surpassing even [[Doge Dark]] and [[Gabriel]] with stats competing with those of [[Wild Doge]]. Those aforementioned stats are exemplified on higher Crown difficulties that double them, in which each Relic Doge will have 150k HP, 24k damage per hit, and over 17k damage per second, becoming a non-negligible threat. As with most Relics, it also has the nasty Curse ability, though this is less relevant than its stats, due to its non-guaranteed activation and short duration.

==Strategy==
Relic Doge's very high stats makes it difficult to simply stall, and it can be a handful in the first few encounters. The use of specialists like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks Cats]] or the [[True Form]] of one of the [[Stories of Legend]] [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] is recommended when dealing with this Doge. [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] could also work as a meatshield, seeing as she is guranteed to survive a hit, no matter the magnification, but Relic Doge's high stats can often make this approach inconsistent.

In its later appearances, however, the introduction of [[Sir Rel]] greatly overshadows Relic Doge's threat, by which point your attackers shouldn't have too much trouble defeating it.

